{
  "nbformat": 4,
  "nbformat_minor": 5,
  "metadata": {
    "kernelspec": {
      "name": "maxima",
      "display_name": "Maxima",
      "language": "maxima"
    },
    "aximar": {}
  },
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "# Heat and Wave Equations by the Method of Lines\n\nThe heat equation $u_t = \\alpha u_{xx}$ and the wave equation $u_{tt} = c^2 u_{xx}$ on $[0, 1]$ with fixed ends both have exact Fourier series solutions. This notebook derives those series symbolically, then solves the same problems numerically by the method of lines: replace $u_{xx}$ with a finite difference on a grid of $N$ interior points, and hand the resulting system of ODEs in time to CVODE.\n\nThe two equations lead to very different ODE systems. The heat equation gives a stiff system: implicit BDF reaches $t = 1$ with about 1300 evaluations of the right-hand side, while explicit Euler needs 20000 steps. The wave equation gives an oscillatory system with purely imaginary eigenvalues, where the non-stiff Adams method is the better choice and conservation of energy checks the result.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "load(\"numerics\")$\nload(\"numerics-sundials\")$\nload(\"ax-plots\")$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 1,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Separation of Variables [S]\n\nSubstituting $u = X(x)\\,T(t)$ into $u_t = \\alpha u_{xx}$ and dividing by $\\alpha X T$ gives $T'/(\\alpha T) = X''/X$. The left side depends only on $t$ and the right only on $x$, so both equal a constant, written $-k^2$. That gives two ODEs, which `ode2` solves.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "assume(k > 0, alpha > 0)$\nsol_X : ode2('diff(X, x, 2) + k^2*X = 0, X, x);\nsol_T : ode2('diff(T, t) = -alpha*k^2*T, T, t);",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 2,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "X = %k1*sin(k*x)+%k2*cos(k*x)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "data": {
            "text/latex": [
              "T=e^ {- \\left(\\alpha\\,k^2\\,t\\right) }\\,{\\it \\%c}"
            ]
          },
          "execution_count": 2,
          "metadata": {},
          "output_type": "execute_result"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "The boundary condition $X(0) = 0$ removes the cosine, and $X(1) = 0$ then requires $\\sin k = 0$, so $k = n\\pi$ for $n = 1, 2, \\dots$ Each mode $\\sin(n\\pi x)\\,e^{-\\alpha n^2\\pi^2 t}$ satisfies the equation exactly, and decays at a rate that grows as $n^2$.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "declare(n, integer)$\nheat_mode : sin(n*%pi*x)*exp(-alpha*n^2*%pi^2*t)$\n'diff(u, t) - alpha*'diff(u, x, 2) = ratsimp(diff(heat_mode, t) - alpha*diff(heat_mode, x, 2));",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 3,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "data": {
            "text/latex": [
              "{{\\partial}\\over{\\partial\\,t}}\\,u-\\alpha\\,\\left({{\\partial^2}\\over{\\partial \\,x^2}}\\,u\\right)=0"
            ]
          },
          "execution_count": 3,
          "metadata": {},
          "output_type": "execute_result"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Fourier Coefficients of a Triangle [S]\n\nThe initial temperature is a triangle with peak 1 at the centre, $f(x) = 1 - |2x - 1|$. The sine coefficients are $b_n = 2\\int_0^1 f(x)\\sin(n\\pi x)\\,dx$, which `integrate` evaluates on each half of the interval.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "b_heat : 2*(integrate(2*x*sin(n*%pi*x), x, 0, 1/2)\n          + integrate(2*(1 - x)*sin(n*%pi*x), x, 1/2, 1))$\nb_heat : trigsimp(ratsimp(b_heat));",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 4,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "data": {
            "text/latex": [
              "{{8\\,\\sin \\left({{\\pi\\,n}\\over{2}}\\right)}\\over{\\pi^2\\,n^2}}"
            ]
          },
          "execution_count": 4,
          "metadata": {},
          "output_type": "execute_result"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "The even coefficients vanish because the triangle is symmetric about $x = 1/2$, and the odd ones alternate in sign and fall as $1/n^2$. The exact solution is the series below.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "print(makelist(subst(n = j, b_heat), j, 1, 7))$\n'u(x, t) = 'sum(b_heat*heat_mode, n, 1, inf);",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 5,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "[8/%pi^2,0,-(8/(9*%pi^2)),0,8/(25*%pi^2),0,-(8/(49*%pi^2))]"
          ]
        },
        {
          "data": {
            "text/latex": [
              "u\\left(x , t\\right)={{8\\,\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty }{{{e^ {- \\left(\\pi^2\\,\\alpha\\,n ^2\\,t\\right) }\\,\\sin \\left({{\\pi\\,n}\\over{2}}\\right)\\,\\sin \\left(\\pi\\,n\\,x \\right)}\\over{n^2}}}}\\over{\\pi^2}}"
            ]
          },
          "execution_count": 5,
          "metadata": {},
          "output_type": "execute_result"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## The Discrete Laplacian [S]\n\nOn a grid $x_i = ih$ with $h = 1/(N+1)$ and $u_0 = u_{N+1} = 0$, the central difference $u_{xx} \\approx (u_{i-1} - 2u_i + u_{i+1})/h^2$ turns the heat equation into $d\\mathbf{u}/dt = \\alpha A\\mathbf{u}$, with $A$ tridiagonal. The grid samples $\\sin(n\\pi x_i)$ of the continuous modes are still eigenvectors of $A$. Applying the difference stencil to them and adding $\\frac{4}{h^2}\\sin^2(n\\pi h/2)$ times the vector leaves zero, which identifies the discrete eigenvalue. Its Taylor series in $h$ shows that it matches the continuous $-n^2\\pi^2$ to second order.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "th : n*%pi*h$\nresidual : (sin((i - 1)*th) - 2*sin(i*th) + sin((i + 1)*th))/h^2\n           + 4/h^2*sin(th/2)^2*sin(i*th)$\nprint(\"Stencil residual:\", trigsimp(trigreduce(trigexpand(residual))))$\nlambda_n : -4/h^2*sin(n*%pi*h/2)^2$\ntaylor(lambda_n, h, 0, 4);",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 6,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Stencil residual: 0"
          ]
        },
        {
          "data": {
            "text/latex": [
              "-\\left(\\pi^2\\,n^2\\right)+{{\\pi^4\\,n^4\\,h^2}\\over{12}}-{{\\pi^6\\,n^6\\,h^4 }\\over{360}}+\\cdots "
            ]
          },
          "execution_count": 6,
          "metadata": {},
          "output_type": "execute_result"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Eigenvalues and Stiffness [N]\n\nWith $N = 99$ ($h = 0.01$) and $\\alpha = 1$, `np_eig` computes the 99 eigenvalues of $A$, which we compare with the formula. The slowest mode decays at nearly $\\pi^2$, while the fastest decays at nearly $4/h^2 = 40000$. The ratio of the two is the stiffness ratio. An explicit method must resolve the fastest rate for stability, even though that mode has died out after a tiny fraction of the time of interest.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "N : 99$\nhv : 1/(N + 1)$\nalpha_v : 1$\nA_mat : genmatrix(lambda([i, j], if i = j then -2 elseif abs(i - j) = 1 then 1 else 0), N, N)/hv^2$\nA_heat : ndarray(float(alpha_v*A_mat))$\n\neig_num : sort(np_to_list(first(np_eig(A_heat))), \">\")$\neig_formula : makelist(float(alpha_v*subst([h = hv, n = k], lambda_n)), k, 1, N)$\nprintf(true, \"Largest relative difference from the formula: ~,2e~%\",\n       lmax(abs((eig_num - eig_formula)/eig_formula)))$\nprintf(true, \"Slowest mode: ~,6f   (continuous -pi^2 = ~,6f)~%\", first(eig_num), float(-%pi^2))$\nprintf(true, \"Fastest mode: ~,2f~%\", last(eig_num))$\nprintf(true, \"Stiffness ratio |lambda_max| / |lambda_min| = ~,1f~%\",\n       last(eig_num)/first(eig_num))$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 7,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Largest relative difference from the formula: 7.36e-13\nSlowest mode: -9.868793   (continuous -pi^2 = -9.869604)\nFastest mode: -39990.13\nStiffness ratio |lambda_max| / |lambda_min| = 4052.2"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Solving with BDF [N]\n\nCVODE's BDF method handles stiff systems. The right-hand side is the method of lines written out: one expression $\\alpha(u_{i-1} - 2u_i + u_{i+1})/h^2$ per grid point, with $u_0 = u_{N+1} = 0$, passed to `np_cvode` with the 99 state variables. Two references check the result at each output time:\n\n- the Fourier series of the PDE, summed to 99 terms, which measures the total error;\n- the exact solution of the ODE system, $\\sum_n \\hat c_n e^{\\lambda_n t}\\mathbf{v}_n$ with the discrete eigenvalues, which isolates the error of the time integration.\n\nBoth references use the matrix $S_{ni} = \\sin(n\\pi x_i)$.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "xs : makelist(float(i*hv), i, 1, N)$\nu0_heat : map(lambda([xv], 1 - abs(2*xv - 1)), xs)$\nS_mat : genmatrix(lambda([m, i], float(sin(m*%pi*i/(N + 1)))), N, N)$\nS_nd : ndarray(S_mat)$\nSt_nd : ndarray(transpose(S_mat))$\nmodes : makelist(k, k, 1, N)$\n\nbn_heat : float(map(lambda([k], subst(n = k, b_heat)), modes))$\nc_hat_heat : np_to_list(np_scale(2.0/(N + 1), np_matmul(S_nd, ndarray(u0_heat))))$\nheat_fourier(tv) := np_to_list(np_matmul(St_nd,\n  ndarray(bn_heat*exp(float(-alpha_v*%pi^2*tv)*modes^2))))$\nheat_semi(tv) := np_to_list(np_matmul(St_nd,\n  ndarray(c_hat_heat*exp(tv*eig_formula))))$\n\nus : makelist(concat(u, i), i, 1, N)$\ngrid_u(i) := if i = 0 or i = N + 1 then 0 else us[i]$\nheat_exprs : makelist(alpha_v*(grid_u(i - 1) - 2*grid_u(i) + grid_u(i + 1))/hv^2, i, 1, N)$\n\nt_heat : [0.0, 0.01, 0.02, 0.05, 0.1, 0.2, 0.5, 1.0]$\nwall0 : elapsed_real_time()$\nsol_bdf : np_cvode(heat_exprs, cons(t, us), u0_heat, t_heat, 1e-8, 1e-10, bdf)$\nprintf(true, \"BDF in expression mode: ~,3f s~%\", elapsed_real_time() - wall0)$\nrows_bdf : args(np_to_matrix(sol_bdf))$\n\nprintf(true, \"  t      max|u|     error vs Fourier   error vs ODE exact~%\")$\nfor row in rest(rows_bdf) do block([tv : first(row), u : rest(row)],\n  printf(true, \"~5,2f  ~10,3e   ~10,3e         ~10,3e~%\", tv, lmax(abs(u)),\n         lmax(abs(u - heat_fourier(tv))), lmax(abs(u - heat_semi(tv)))))$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 8,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "BDF in expression mode: 0.058 s\n  t      max|u|     error vs Fourier   error vs ODE exact\n 0.01    7.745e-1     1.412e-4           1.233e-8\n 0.02    6.809e-1     9.979e-5           6.189e-9\n 0.05    4.960e-1     6.508e-5           6.381e-9\n 0.10    3.022e-1     4.947e-5           1.352e-9\n 0.20    1.126e-1     2.755e-5           3.240e-9\n 0.50    5.832e-3     2.847e-6          8.620e-10\n 1.00    4.196e-5     3.772e-8          2.264e-10"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "The time integration error stays at the level of CVODE's tolerances, $10^{-8}$ relative and $10^{-10}$ absolute. The error against the Fourier series is about $2\\times 10^{-4}$ of the peak value early on, and comes from the spatial grid. The discrete eigenvalues differ from $-n^2\\pi^2$ by about $n^4\\pi^4 h^2/12$, and the high modes, which the grid represents worst, carry the corner of the triangle. The error shrinks as those modes decay.\n\nThe snapshots show the corner rounding off at once, then the profile relaxing to the shape of the slowest mode, $\\sin \\pi x$, as it decays. Points are the method of lines, curves the Fourier series.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "x_plot : np_to_list(np_linspace(0.0, 1.0, 201))$\nheat_series_at(tv) := map(lambda([xv],\n  float(sum(bn_heat[k]*exp(-alpha_v*%pi^2*k^2*tv)*sin(k*%pi*xv), k, 1, 49))), x_plot)$\npad(u) := append([0.0], u, [0.0])$\nx_full : pad(xs)$\nsnap_cols : [\"steelblue\", \"darkorange\", \"seagreen\", \"crimson\", \"purple\"]$\nsnap_rows : [1, 2, 4, 5, 6]$\n\napply(ax_draw2d, append(\n  apply(append, makelist(block([row : rows_bdf[snap_rows[k]]],\n    [color = snap_cols[k], marker_size = 4, name = printf(false, \"MOL t = ~,2f\", first(row)),\n     points(makelist(x_full[2*j - 1], j, 1, 51), makelist(pad(rest(row))[2*j - 1], j, 1, 51)),\n     line_width = 2, name = printf(false, \"Fourier t = ~,2f\", first(row)),\n     lines(x_plot, if first(row) = 0.0 then map(lambda([xv], 1 - abs(2*xv - 1)), x_plot)\n                   else heat_series_at(first(row)))]), k, 1, 5)),\n  [title = \"Heat Equation: Method of Lines and Fourier Series\", xlabel = \"x\", ylabel = \"u\",\n   grid = true, showlegend = true]))$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 9,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "data": {
            "application/x-maxima-plotly": [
