0348,0.04455942829193572,0.047821442186590325,0.05088694751812877,0.05374334746749975,0.05637890447450543,0.05878278846995816,0.06094512137876214,0.06285701771104761,0.06451062107455938,0.06589913645826233,0.06701685815450377,0.06785919320499377,0.06842268027425949,0.06870500387301737,0.06870500387301737,0.06842268027425949,0.06785919320499378,0.06701685815450377,0.06589913645826233,0.06451062107455939,0.06285701771104762,0.060945121378762145,0.058782788469958165,0.05637890447450544,0.05374334746749977,0.050886947518128785,0.04782144218659033,0.044559428291935724,0.04111431014903485,0.03750024448736811,0.03373208227798664,0.029825307707685267,0.025795974551157466,0.0216606402025921,0.01743629763779074,0.013140305586387447,0.008790317201108296,0.004404207517183992,3.894509649490062e-17]],\"type\":\"surface\",\"name\":\"-(5.329187831286668e-4*%e^-(1521*%pi^2*t)*sin(39*%pi*x))+5.920887283701258e-4*%e^-(1369*%pi^2*t)*sin(37*%pi*x)-6.616893625622059e-4*%e^-(1225*%pi^2*t)*sin(35*%pi*x)+7.443245813945842e-4*%e^-(1089*%pi^2*t)*sin(33*%pi*x)-8.434645880735715e-4*%e^-(961*%pi^2*t)*sin(31*%pi*x)+9.638162534348421e-4*%e^-(841*%pi^2*t)*sin(29*%pi*x)-0.0011118922759104281*%e^-(729*%pi^2*t)*sin(27*%pi*x)+0.0012969111506219236*%e^-(625*%pi^2*t)*sin(25*%pi*x)-0.0015322674274833691*%e^-(529*%pi^2*t)*sin(23*%pi*x)+0.0018380260071172386*%e^-(441*%pi^2*t)*sin(21*%pi*x)-0.0022453447898579007*%e^-(361*%pi^2*t)*sin(19*%pi*x)+0.002804738647538762*%e^-(289*%pi^2*t)*sin(17*%pi*x)-0.0036025309739497876*%e^-(225*%pi^2*t)*sin(15*%pi*x)+0.004796269048158001*%e^-(169*%pi^2*t)*sin(13*%pi*x)-0.006698921232551258*%e^-(121*%pi^2*t)*sin(11*%pi*x)+0.010007030483193853*%e^-(81*%pi^2*t)*sin(9*%pi*x)-0.016542234064055146*%e^-(49*%pi^2*t)*sin(7*%pi*x)+0.03242277876554809*%e^-(25*%pi^2*t)*sin(5*%pi*x)-0.09006327434874468*%e^-(9*%pi^2*t)*sin(3*%pi*x)+0.8105694691387022*%e^-(%pi^2*t)*sin(%pi*x)\"}],\"layout\":{\"title\":{\"text\":\"Heat Equation u(x, t)\"},\"width\":700,\"height\":450,\"paper_bgcolor\":\"white\",\"scene\":{\"bgcolor\":\"white\",\"xaxis\":{\"title\":{\"text\":\"x\"},\"gridcolor\":\"#ddd\",\"linecolor\":\"#ddd\",\"linewidth\":1,\"zerolinecolor\":\"black\",\"zerolinewidth\":1},\"yaxis\":{\"title\":{\"text\":\"t\"},\"gridcolor\":\"#ddd\",\"linecolor\":\"#ddd\",\"linewidth\":1,\"zerolinecolor\":\"black\",\"zerolinewidth\":1},\"zaxis\":{\"title\":{\"text\":\"u\"},\"gridcolor\":\"#ddd\",\"linecolor\":\"#ddd\",\"linewidth\":1,\"zerolinecolor\":\"black\",\"zerolinewidth\":1}}}}"
            ]
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "output_type": "display_data"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## The Cost of Stiffness [N]\n\nThe same problem with CVODE's Adams method, which is explicit in character and suits non-stiff problems, needs several times as many right-hand-side evaluations. To count them, this section passes the right-hand side as a function, the matrix product $\\alpha A\\mathbf{u}$, which adds one to a counter on every call. The counts include the evaluations CVODE spends building finite-difference Jacobians.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "heat_rhs(tv, y) := (rhs_calls : rhs_calls + 1, np_to_list(np_matmul(A_heat, y)))$\n\nrhs_calls : 0$\nwall0 : elapsed_real_time()$\nsol_bdf_fn : np_cvode(heat_rhs, u0_heat, t_heat, 1e-8, 1e-10, bdf, 100000)$\nwall_bdf : elapsed_real_time() - wall0$\ncalls_bdf : rhs_calls$\n\nrhs_calls : 0$\nwall0 : elapsed_real_time()$\nsol_adams : np_cvode(heat_rhs, u0_heat, t_heat, 1e-8, 1e-10, adams, 100000)$\nwall_adams : elapsed_real_time() - wall0$\ncalls_adams : rhs_calls$\nprintf(true, \"BDF:   ~6d right-hand-side calls, ~,3f s~%\", calls_bdf, wall_bdf)$\nprintf(true, \"Adams: ~6d right-hand-side calls, ~,3f s~%\", calls_adams, wall_adams)$\nprintf(true, \"Adams and BDF agree at t = 1 to ~,2e~%\",\n       lmax(abs(rest(last(args(np_to_matrix(sol_adams)))) - rest(last(rows_bdf)))))$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 11,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "BDF:     1317 right-hand-side calls, 0.020 s\nAdams:  12959 right-hand-side calls, 0.255 s\nAdams and BDF agree at t = 1 to 7.31e-10"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "Explicit Euler, $\\mathbf{u}_{k+1} = \\mathbf{u}_k + \\Delta t\\,\\alpha A\\mathbf{u}_k$, makes the point more plainly. It is stable only while $|1 + \\Delta t\\,\\lambda| \\le 1$ for every eigenvalue, which for the fastest mode means $\\Delta t \\le 2/|\\lambda_{\\max}|$, just above $h^2/(2\\alpha) = 5\\times 10^{-5}$. Reaching $t = 1$ at that step takes 20000 steps. With a step 10% larger, the fastest mode grows by a factor of about 1.2 per step, starting from rounding error.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "euler_heat(dt, tend) := block([u : ndarray(u0_heat), steps : round(tend/dt)],\n  for k : 1 thru steps do u : np_add(u, np_scale(dt, np_matmul(A_heat, u))),\n  [steps, np_to_list(u)])$\n\ndt_lim : float(hv^2/(2*alpha_v))$\n[steps_ok, u_ok] : euler_heat(dt_lim, 1.0)$\nprintf(true, \"dt = ~,2e: ~d steps, error vs Fourier at t = 1: ~,2e (max|u| = ~,2e)~%\",\n       dt_lim, steps_ok, lmax(abs(u_ok - heat_fourier(1.0))), lmax(abs(u_ok)))$\nprintf(true, \"Growth factor of the fastest mode at 1.1 dt: ~,4f~%\", abs(1 + 1.1*dt_lim*last(eig_num)))$\n[steps_bad, u_bad] : euler_heat(1.1*dt_lim, 0.1)$\nprintf(true, \"dt = ~,2e: ~d steps to t = 0.1, max|u| = ~,2e~%\", 1.1*dt_lim, steps_bad, lmax(abs(u_bad)))$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 12,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "dt = 5.00e-5: 20000 steps, error vs Fourier at t = 1: 7.49e-8 (max|u| = 4.19e-5)\nGrowth factor of the fastest mode at 1.1 dt: 1.1995\ndt = 5.50e-5: 1818 steps to t = 0.1, max|u| = 7.87e+139"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## The Plucked String [S]\n\nA string of length 1 is pulled aside to height $a$ at $x = p$ and released from rest. The initial shape is two straight segments. The same separation of variables gives modes $\\sin(n\\pi x)\\cos(n\\pi c t)$, and `integrate` gives the coefficients for a general pluck point.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "assume(0 < p, p < 1)$\nb_wave : 2*(integrate(a*x/p*sin(n*%pi*x), x, 0, p)\n          + integrate(a*(1 - x)/(1 - p)*sin(n*%pi*x), x, p, 1))$\nb_wave : factor(ratsimp(b_wave));",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 13,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "data": {
            "text/latex": [
              "-\\left({{2\\,a\\,\\sin \\left(\\pi\\,n\\,p\\right)}\\over{\\pi^2\\,n^2\\,\\left(p-1 \\right)\\,p}}\\right)"
            ]
          },
          "execution_count": 13,
          "metadata": {},
          "output_type": "execute_result"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "Modes with a node at the pluck point, where $\\sin(n\\pi p) = 0$, are absent. Each standing wave splits into two travelling waves, which is d'Alembert's form of the solution: $u = \\frac12[F(x - ct) + F(x + ct)]$, where $F$ is the initial shape extended to an odd function of period 2. With `gradef` declaring the derivatives of an arbitrary $F$, Maxima confirms that this form solves the wave equation and starts at rest.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "print(\"Mode:\", trigreduce(sin(n*%pi*x)*cos(n*%pi*c*t)))$\ngradef(F(s), F1(s))$\ngradef(F1(s), F2(s))$\nu_dal : (F(x - c*t) + F(x + c*t))/2$\nprint(\"u_tt - c^2 u_xx =\", expand(diff(u_dal, t, 2) - c^2*diff(u_dal, x, 2)))$\nprint(\"u_t at t = 0:   \", subst(t = 0, diff(u_dal, t)))$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 14,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Mode: sin(%pi*n*x+%pi*c*n*t)/2+sin(%pi*n*x-%pi*c*n*t)/2\nu_tt - c^2 u_xx = 0\nu_t at t = 0:    0"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## The String as a First-Order System [N]\n\nWith velocity $\\mathbf{v} = \\dot{\\mathbf{u}}$ the semi-discrete wave equation becomes the first-order system\n\n$$\\frac{d}{dt}\\begin{pmatrix}\\mathbf{u}\\\\ \\mathbf{v}\\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix}0 & I\\\\ c^2 A & 0\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}\\mathbf{u}\\\\ \\mathbf{v}\\end{pmatrix}$$\n\nof 198 equations. Its eigenvalues are $\\pm i\\omega_n$ with $\\omega_n = (2c/h)\\sin(n\\pi h/2)$, all on the imaginary axis, so nothing decays and Adams is the natural method. The string is plucked at $p = 0.3$ with $a = 1$ and $c = 1$, so one period takes $t = 2$.\n\nd'Alembert's formula gives the exact PDE solution, and the discrete modes give the exact solution of the ODE system, $\\mathbf{u}(t) = \\sum_n \\hat c_n\\cos(\\omega_n t)\\,\\mathbf{v}_n$.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "c_v : 1$\np_v : 3/10$\nM_wave : ndarray(float(addrow(addcol(zeromatrix(N, N), ident(N)),\n                              addcol(c_v^2*A_mat, zeromatrix(N, N)))))$\nwave_rhs(tv, y) := (rhs_calls : rhs_calls + 1, np_to_list(np_matmul(M_wave, y)))$\n\npluck(xv) := if xv <= p_v then float(xv/p_v) else float((1 - xv)/(1 - p_v))$\npluck_odd(xv) := block([xm : xv - 2*floor((xv + 1)/2)],\n  if xm >= 0 then pluck(xm) else -pluck(-xm))$\ndalembert(xv, tv) := (pluck_odd(xv - c_v*tv) + pluck_odd(xv + c_v*tv))/2$\n\nu0_wave : map(pluck, xs)$\nomega : makelist(float(2*c_v/hv*sin(k*%pi*hv/2)), k, 1, N)$\nc_hat_wave : np_to_list(np_scale(2.0/(N + 1), np_matmul(S_nd, ndarray(u0_wave))))$\nwave_semi(tv) := np_to_list(np_matmul(St_nd, ndarray(c_hat_wave*cos(tv*omega))))$\n\nt_wave : np_to_list(np_linspace(0.0, 2.0, 81))$\ny0_wave : append(u0_wave, makelist(0.0, i, 1, N))$\nrhs_calls : 0$\nwall0 : elapsed_real_time()$\nsol_wave : np_cvode(wave_rhs, y0_wave, t_wave, 1e-8, 1e-10, adams, 100000)$\nprintf(true, \"Adams: ~d right-hand-side calls, ~,3f s~%\", rhs_calls, elapsed_real_time() - wall0)$\nrows_wave : args(np_to_matrix(sol_wave))$\n\nprintf(true, \"  t     error vs d'Alembert   error vs ODE exact~%\")$\nfor k in [11, 21, 41, 61, 81] do block([row : rows_wave[k], tv, u],\n  tv : first(row), u : makelist(row[i + 1], i, 1, N),\n  printf(true, \"~5,2f   ~10,3e            ~10,3e~%\", tv,\n         lmax(abs(u - map(lambda([xv], dalembert(xv, tv)), xs))),\n         lmax(abs(u - wave_semi(tv)))))$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 15,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Adams: 9374 right-hand-side calls, 0.326 s\n  t     error vs d'Alembert   error vs ODE exact\n 0.25     8.688e-3              6.418e-9\n 0.50     1.173e-2              9.293e-9\n 1.00     2.778e-2              1.080e-8\n 1.50     1.653e-2              1.120e-8\n 2.00     3.637e-2              1.116e-8"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "Adams follows the ODE system to about $10^{-8}$. The larger error against d'Alembert's solution comes from the grid: the discrete frequencies $\\omega_n$ fall below $n\\pi c$ for high $n$, so the short waves that make up each corner travel too slowly and trail ripples behind it. The ripples show in the snapshots, where curves are d'Alembert's solution and points the method of lines. At $t = 1$ the string is the initial shape reflected through $x = 1/2$ and turned upside down.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "apply(ax_draw2d, append(\n  apply(append, makelist(block([row : rows_wave[[1, 11, 21, 41][k]], tv],\n    tv : first(row),\n    [color = snap_cols[k], marker_size = 4, name = printf(false, \"MOL t = ~,2f\", tv),\n     points(x_full, pad(makelist(row[i + 1], i, 1, N))),\n     line_width = 2, name = printf(false, \"exact t = ~,2f\", tv),\n     lines(x_plot, map(lambda([xv], dalembert(xv, tv)), x_plot))]), k, 1, 4)),\n  [title = \"Plucked String: Method of Lines and d'Alembert\", xlabel = \"x\", ylabel = \"u\",\n   grid = true, showlegend = true]))$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 16,
      "outputs": [
        {
