    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Energy Conservation [S+N]\n\nThe energy of the string, $E = \\frac12\\int_0^1 (u_t^2 + c^2 u_x^2)\\,dx$, stays constant. At $t = 0$ only the potential term contributes, and the slopes $a/p$ and $-a/(1-p)$ give $E = c^2a^2/(2p(1-p))$. The semi-discrete system conserves the matching sum\n\n$$E_h = \\frac h2\\sum_i v_i^2 + \\frac{c^2}{2h}\\sum_{i=0}^{N}(u_{i+1} - u_i)^2$$\n\nexactly, and its initial value equals the continuous one because the pluck point sits on the grid. Any drift in $E_h$ measures the time integrator. BDF, run on the same problem, damps the oscillation slightly, because its higher orders are not stable all the way along the imaginary axis.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "E_exact : subst([a = 1, p = p_v, c = c_v], c^2*a^2/(2*p*(1 - p)));\nstring_energy(row) := block([u : pad(makelist(row[i + 1], i, 1, N)), v : makelist(row[N + 1 + i], i, 1, N)],\n  float(hv/2*apply(\"+\", v^2) + c_v^2/(2*hv)*apply(\"+\", makelist((u[i + 1] - u[i])^2, i, 1, N + 1))))$\n\nrhs_calls : 0$\nsol_wave_bdf : np_cvode(wave_rhs, y0_wave, t_wave, 1e-8, 1e-10, bdf, 100000)$\ncalls_wave_bdf : rhs_calls$\nE_adams : map(string_energy, rows_wave)$\nE_bdf : map(string_energy, args(np_to_matrix(sol_wave_bdf)))$\nprintf(true, \"E exact = ~,10f, E_h(0) = ~,10f~%\", float(E_exact), first(E_adams))$\nprintf(true, \"Adams: max |E_h(t) - E_h(0)| = ~,2e, change over one period ~,2e~%\",\n       lmax(abs(E_adams - first(E_adams))), last(E_adams) - first(E_adams))$\nprintf(true, \"BDF:   max |E_h(t) - E_h(0)| = ~,2e, change over one period ~,2e~%\",\n       lmax(abs(E_bdf - first(E_bdf))), last(E_bdf) - first(E_bdf))$\nprintf(true, \"BDF used ~d right-hand-side calls~%\", calls_wave_bdf)$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 17,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "50/21\nE exact = 2.3809523810, E_h(0) = 2.3809523810\nAdams: max |E_h(t) - E_h(0)| = 2.13e-7, change over one period 2.13e-7\nBDF:   max |E_h(t) - E_h(0)| = 3.17e-6, change over one period -3.17e-6\nBDF used 28397 right-hand-side calls"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "Adams gains about $2\\times 10^{-7}$ of energy over the period. BDF loses fifteen times as much and needs three times as many right-hand-side calls, so it gains nothing on an oscillatory problem. The plot shows the energy error over one period for both methods.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "ax_draw2d(\n  color = \"steelblue\", line_width = 2, name = \"Adams\",\n  lines(t_wave, abs(E_adams - first(E_adams)) + 1e-16),\n  color = \"crimson\", name = \"BDF\",\n  lines(t_wave, abs(E_bdf - first(E_bdf)) + 1e-16),\n  logy = true, title = \"Energy Error of the Semi-Discrete String\",\n  xlabel = \"t\", ylabel = \"|E_h(t) - E_h(0)|\", grid = true, showlegend = true)$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 18,
      "outputs": [
