    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Summary\n\n| Step | Method |\n|------|--------|\n| Separated modes | Symbolic: `ode2` for $X$ and $T$, boundary conditions give $k = n\\pi$ |\n| Heat coefficients | Symbolic: `integrate` over each half of the triangle, $b_n = 8\\sin(n\\pi/2)/(n\\pi)^2$ |\n| Discrete eigenvalues | Symbolic stencil identity, Taylor series in $h$; numeric `np_eig` check |\n| Stiffness | Numeric: ratio of about 4000 for $N = 99$ |\n| Heat solution | Numeric: `np_cvode` with BDF on 99 grid-point expressions, checked against the Fourier series and the exact ODE solution |\n| Cost of stiffness | Numeric: Adams call count, explicit Euler at and beyond its stability limit |\n| Plucked string | Symbolic: coefficients for any pluck point, d'Alembert form checked with `gradef` |\n| Wave solution | Numeric: `np_cvode` with Adams on a 198-equation system, checked against d'Alembert |\n| Energy | Exact initial energy; drift of the discrete energy for Adams and BDF |\n| Animation | Fourier series of the string over one period |",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## References\n\n- E. M. Stein and R. Shakarchi, *Fourier Analysis: An Introduction*, Chapter 1: the wave equation and d'Alembert's solution (§1.2), the plucked string (§1.3), and the heat equation (§2).",
      "metadata": {}
    }
  ]
}